# Line endings: the repo is stored and checked out as LF everywhere.
# Why it matters here:
#   - shell scripts (scripts/*.sh) MUST stay LF, or Linux/macOS bash fails with
#     "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env sh^M";
#   - the PowerShell validator must keep its UTF-8 BOM (tracked as file content,
#     untouched by these rules) or Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes it as ANSI and
#     the Chinese V11 literals silently stop matching.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
